page='''<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The Rough Riders | Flight & Combat Guide</title><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="art/badge.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head>
<body><a class="skip" href="#pilot">Skip to pilot guide</a><header><a href="#top" aria-label="Rough Riders home"><img src="art/wordmark.png" alt="The Rough Riders"></a><nav aria-label="Page sections"><a href="#pilot">Pilot files</a><a href="#squad">Squad play</a><a href="#decisions">Open decisions</a></nav><span class="build">BOF / STAGE 06 / CURRENT BUILD</span></header>
<main id="top"><section class="hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">FIVE PILOTS. FIVE DISTINCT THREATS.</p><h1>Know who you’re<br>flying against.</h1><p class="lede">Their identities, flight patterns, tells and attacks — with video from the actual game.</p><p class="small">Furious previews · Native game renderer and audio · Individually staged move demonstrations</p><a class="primary" href="#pilot">Open pilot files <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><img src="art/crew_photo.png" alt="Voss, Nyx, Rook, Kaia and Jace with their own aircraft behind them"></section>
<section id="pilot" aria-labelledby="pilot-heading"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">01 / PILOT FILES</p><h2 id="pilot-heading">The five riders</h2><p>Choose a pilot. Jump straight to a move below the video.</p></div><div class="pilot-layout"><aside aria-label="Choose a pilot" id="roster"></aside><div class="pilot-body"><div class="pilot-heading"><img id="portrait" alt=""><div><p class="eyebrow" id="role"></p><h2 id="name"></h2><p id="ship"></p></div><img id="ship-art" alt=""></div><p id="identity"></p><blockquote id="quote"></blockquote><div class="screen"><video id="player" controls playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Pilot flight and attack preview"></video><div class="video-label"><span id="clip-label">CURRENT BUILD / FURIOUS</span><button type="button" id="replay">Replay preview</button></div></div><div id="chapters" class="chapters" aria-label="Video chapters"></div><p class="evidence-note">These are isolated demonstrations: native attack controllers run at normal speed in the real game. Other pilots’ automatic attacks and allies are held back for clarity. The observer uses GOD mode. Reveal and interception events are deliberately triggered where labelled.</p><div class="intent-grid"><article><h3>What this pilot asks of you</h3><p id="purpose"></p></article><article><h3>How the aircraft moves</h3><p id="flight"></p></article></div><div id="attacks"></div></div></div></section>
<section id="squad"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">02 / SQUAD PLAY</p><h2>Five ships, one encounter.</h2><p>The shared flight language and the attacks they perform together.</p></div><div class="shared-grid"><article class="panel"><h3>The new airshow entrance</h3><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" src="entrance.mp4" poster="art/crew_photo.png" aria-label="Live Rough Riders entrance"></video><p>Catch-up northbound → turbo exit → two somersault passes each → crossing airshow → bowling formation → slow drifting dialogue. The introduction stays protected until combat begins.</p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Cruise, bank, evade, recover</h3><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" src="videos/evasion/preview.mp4" poster="videos/evasion/poster.jpg" aria-label="Shared flight and barrel roll preview"></video><p>The combat controller sways each aircraft within its lane. Nearby incoming fire can trigger a short lateral barrel roll, followed by a return to cruise. The opener’s somersaults are separate from this combat evasion.</p></article></div><article class="panel formation"><div><p class="eyebrow">COORDINATED MISSILE TURN</p><h3>Lock, volley, scatter, return.</h3><p>All living pilots assemble and place Retina locks on their targets. Each launches two physical missiles. The crew then splits toward north/south edges and returns on continuous flight paths.</p><p>Missiles can be shot down. Their homing phase commits near the target or after 0.9 seconds; the lock warning belongs on the victim.</p><p class="notice">Current-build finding: Star, Bowling, H and X calls all use the same staggered volley layout. The bowling formation in the new introduction is distinct and already works.</p></div><div><video id="formation-video" controls playsinline preload="metadata" src="videos/formations/preview.mp4" poster="videos/formations/poster.jpg" aria-label="Four formation calls and their native missile volleys"></video><div class="chapters" id="formation-chapters"></div></div></article><div class="intent-grid"><article><h3>Shared firing pressure</h3><p>The current tuning gives one background gun turn at a time and suppresses those shots during heavy specials. Furious can admit two special controllers, with additional interlocks preventing some heavy combinations. The resulting pressure is deliberately shared rather than five independent streams.</p></article><article><h3>What can you destroy?</h3><p>Physical homing missiles, Kaia’s rollers and the defined energy objects are destructible. Rook’s ordinary chaingun slugs are not. Do not treat every bright projectile as a shootable missile.</p></article><article><h3>Their stolen equipment</h3><p>Personal supply boxes can arm the next selection. Destroying one delays that pilot’s special. The isolated previews begin directly at move selection so every attack is easy to inspect.</p></article><article><h3>Decker’s counterplay</h3><p>The full crew encounter also has Decker’s supply-box shield event: opening the box casts a temporary central divider that reflects ordnance. This support event is suppressed in the individual previews so it does not obscure their patterns.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="decisions"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">03 / NEXT DESIGN DECISIONS</p><h2>Keep the identities. Resolve the gaps.</h2><p>These are findings and suggested directions, not changes to the game in this pass.</p></div><div class="decision-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Give Rook three real choices</h3><p>Keep the dual chaingun, restore a distinct warned charge dash, and decide whether the physical hook belongs in his final move set. Today all three selections collapse into the chaingun.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Make the formation names mean different shapes</h3><p>Use actual Star, Bowling, H and X arrangements with separate travel lanes and readable missile timing. Today they share one layout.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Lock Kaia’s final weapon identity</h3><p>Her live teal roller gatling is distinct. The earlier slower five-way wind spread is not her current attack. Choose whether to retain the roller burst or give her a separate fan turn.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Finish Nyx’s shadow language</h3><p>Cloak, reveal and retaliation are present. The shared energy throttle reduces her intended three-way releases to one charge per pulse, and the current effect palette still leans cyan. Dark-purple shadow energy would better match her hull.</p></div></article></div></section>
<footer><img src="art/badge.png" alt="Rough Riders crew patch"><div><strong>THE ROUGH RIDERS / FLIGHT & COMBAT GUIDE</strong><p>Current game behavior, October 28, 2026. No combat changes in this guide.</p><p><a href="evidence.json">Verification & recording notes</a> · <a href="inventory.json">Observed selection mapping</a> · <a href="data.json">Pilot guide data</a></p></div></footer></main><script src="app.js"></script></body></html>'''
